<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-Singapore May industrial output down 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Singapore May industrial output down 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total manufacturing output fell by 1.6 percent in May compared to the same month the year before, after rising a revised 1.4 percent in April, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said on Monday.  </p>
<p>Table of selected Singapore industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				     May 97	Apr 97	  Mar 97</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	 -1.6	   1.4	    -6.7</p>
<p>    Electronics		   -0.1	   3.9	   -11.6</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	   0.2	 -13.6	   -14.3</p>
<p>    Pharmaceuticals	    -12.2	  13.3	    -4.6</p>
<p>    Industrial chemicals	 8.7	  14.7	    13.8</p>
<p>    Petrochemicals		33.6	  11.1	    29.2</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics   -5.2	  -2.1	     3.9</p>
<p>    Transport equipment	 -0.4	   6.0	     1.3</p>
<p>    Fabricated metals	  -14.7	 -11.5	   -10.7</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	  8.3	   5.9	     1.0</p>
<p>    Food &amp; Beverages	    -4.3	  -1.1	   -12.0</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	  3.2	  -1.7	     0.0</p>
<p>    Plastic products	    -7.2	  -8.5	   -18.3</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
